id: pm-jd2zim
title: "Lock GC sweep, stale-lock reclaim and the post-create entry check act by pathname after a one-time confinement check, so a mid-operation lock-directory swap can reach outside the tracker"
description: "Lock GC sweep, post-EEXIST stale reclaim and the post-create entry check re-resolve lock paths after pm-gh1647's one-time confinement check, so a concurrent lock-directory swap can make pm read or unlink outside the tracker. Bind those steps to the verified directory (Linux procfs dirfd) and refuse wherever binding is unavailable; a pathname re-check is not a fix."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: confinement,locks,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-11-01T15:40:08.751Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T09:29:57.622Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "pm gc --scope locks never unlinks or reads a lock entry outside the tracker when locks/ is swapped for a symlink during the sweep, proven by a regression test that swaps the directory between readdir and removal; The post-EEXIST stale-lock reclaim never reads, gates or unlinks through a replaced lock directory and refuses with lock_path_unsafe when the directory identity changed since creation, proven by a swap regression test; verifyConfinedLockCreation binds its entry check to the verified directory (Linux procfs dirfd) so a hard-linked inode in a swapped outside directory cannot pass, and other platforms refuse when identity cannot be bound; assertLockEntryNotSymlink treats only ENOENT as absent while preserving the Windows EPERM, EACCES and EBUSY delete-pending waits; docs/SDK.md states the exact confinement guarantee per operation and platform; When the post-open entry check refuses with lock_path_unsafe after a late swap, the SDK removes the lock file it just created only if that path still names the inode of the opened descriptor (verified through the bound directory, never by a fresh pathname lookup), so no empty lock file is left outside the tracker and no file pm did not create is ever unlinked, proven by the GH-1652 late-swap regression (fs.open mocked to swap locks/ just before the wx open)"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
expected_result: "Every destructive lock step (gc sweep unlink, stale reclaim read/gate/unlink, lease release) stays bound to the lock directory identity verified at the start, or refuses with lock_path_unsafe when that identity no longer holds"
actual_result: "Only the initial lock-directory check and the post-create identity comparison are confined. Later reads, gates and unlinks re-resolve the pathname and follow a directory swapped mid-operation"
